status: active
goal: Create combined spot-long/perp-short variants of s65, s72, s62 to eliminate funding drag on long positions while keeping perp for shorts
priority: HIGH — s65/s72/s62 are top P&L contributors, funding drag is measurable
started: 2026-03-15
type: strategy development (Class A → Gate 0→1→2→3→4→5→6→7)

trigger: |
  Paper trading shows s65/s72/s62 are our top earners ($174K combined closed P&L)
  but all trade PERP ONLY. Their longs pay funding (currently -$6,655 across open
  positions). On spot these longs would pay ZERO funding.

  Key insight: these strategies go long ~95% of the time. By switching longs to
  spot and keeping shorts on perp (where shorts RECEIVE funding when rates are
  positive), we get the best of both worlds.

hypothesis: |
  "Using spot for long entries and perp for short entries on s65/s62/s72 will
  improve net returns by eliminating funding drag on longs (~0.4-0.7% of notional)
  while maintaining identical signal logic, because funding rates are structurally
  positive (longs pay shorts) in crypto perpetuals."

funding_analysis: |
  From live paper trading (as of 2026-03-15, ~144 ticks):

  | Strategy | Open Notional | Funding Paid | As % Notional | Direction |
  |----------|--------------|-------------|---------------|-----------|
  | s65      | $868K        | -$3,612     | -0.42%        | 100% long |
  | s72      | $461K        | -$3,043     | -0.66%        | 100% long |
  | s62      | $223K        | -$878       | -0.39%        | ~93% long |
  | s57      | $841K        | +$97        | +0.01%        | delta-neutral |

  Annualized funding drag estimate (if rates stay similar):
  - s65: ~$3.6K/week × 52 = ~$187K/year on $868K notional = ~21% APR drag
  - This is MASSIVE — nearly as much as the strategy earns

  Note: funding rates fluctuate. In bull markets they're higher (longs pay more).
  In bear markets they can go negative (longs receive). The structural bias is
  positive rates ~70% of the time.

tradeoffs: |
  ADVANTAGES of spot longs:
  1. Zero funding cost (biggest win)
  2. No liquidation risk on longs (own the asset outright)
  3. No margin requirements for longs (1:1 with capital)
  4. Simpler position management

  DISADVANTAGES of spot longs:
  1. Lower liquidity on some tokens (spot < perp for many alts)
  2. No leverage available (1x only, vs perp which can be 2-5x)
  3. Different fee tiers (spot maker/taker may differ from futures)
  4. Cannot short on spot (need perp for that)
  5. Some tokens may not have spot pairs on Binance
  6. Wider spreads on less liquid spot pairs

  LIQUIDITY CONCERN:
  Must check: for each token s65/s62/s72 trade, compare spot vs perp ADV.
  If spot ADV < 50% of perp ADV, the slippage increase may eat the funding savings.
  Tokens like BTC/ETH/SOL: spot liquidity is fine.
  Tokens like PIPPIN/VVV/KAVA: spot liquidity may be much thinner.

implementation: |
  APPROACH: "combined" market type strategies (like s57 does)

  s57 already uses MarketType.COMBINED — it goes long spot + short perp simultaneously
  for delta-neutral carry. We want a simpler version:
  - When signal says LONG → enter on SPOT
  - When signal says SHORT → enter on PERP
  - Signal logic is IDENTICAL to the base strategy

  This is a Class C overlay (wrapper strategy), NOT a new signal:

  strategies/s86_s65_spot_long.py:
    from strategies.s65_funding_carry_v4 import strategy as base
    def strategy(ctx):
        result = base(ctx)
        if result.direction == 1:  # long
            result.market_type = MarketType.SPOT
        else:  # short
            result.market_type = MarketType.PERP
        return result

  strategies/s87_s62_spot_long.py: same pattern wrapping s62
  strategies/s88_s72_spot_long.py: same pattern wrapping s72

  CRITICAL: Check if these strategies ever go short. If they're 100% long-only,
  we can simplify to just MarketType.SPOT (no conditional needed).

liquidity_check: |
  Must verify BEFORE Gate 3 for tokens these strategies actually trade:

  Tokens traded by s65/s72/s62 in paper trading:
  AIXBT, AXS, BERA, DOT, ICP, IP, KAVA, MOODENG, PIPPIN, RENDER,
  TRUMP, VIRTUAL, VVV, ZRO

  For each: compare spot vs perp 24h volume on Binance.
  If spot volume < $1M/day for a token, flag it — may need to skip spot
  for that token and fall back to perp.

  Tool: can use ccxt to fetch 24h volume for both spot and perp pairs.

validation_plan: |
  Gate 0: ✅ Hypothesis clear, economic mechanism sound (funding drag elimination)
  Gate 2: Check overlap with s57 (also combined) — different signal, should pass dedup
  Gate 3: Create wrapper strategies (s86/s87/s88)
  Gate 4: Quick validate on BTC — but these are altcoin strategies, may need different token
  Gate 5: Full validate — compare s86 vs s65, s87 vs s62, s88 vs s72
           Key metric: Calmar improvement from funding savings
           Must also check: does spot slippage eat the funding benefit?
  Gate 6: Deploy to paper trading alongside existing perp-only versions

  COMPARISON METHODOLOGY:
  Run IDENTICAL backtest periods with spot-long vs perp-only.
  The ONLY difference should be:
  - Funding costs (spot-long = 0 on longs)
  - Slippage (spot may be higher for illiquid tokens)
  - Fee differences (spot vs futures fee tiers)

  If net improvement > 5% Calmar → deploy.
  If improvement < 2% → not worth the added complexity.

